}\\end{aligned}]\\in Π.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2} \\\\ 2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}+{b}_{2} \\\\ (2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2})+(2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}+{b}_{2} \\\\ 2({a}_{1}+{b}_{1})-({a}_{2}+{b}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $z=2x-y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in Π.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in Π$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}k{a}_{1} \\\\ k{a}_{2} \\\\ k(2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}k{a}_{1} \\\\ k{a}_{2} \\\\ 2(k{a}_{1})-k{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $z=2x-y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in Π.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since statements II and III are true, $Π$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321933 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321934 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321935 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321936 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321937 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1041 "selection" 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321935 13194139534949 true] [17592186321932 1110 #uuid "53c5b6cc-2be2-51e2-98b3-6996390b7483" 13194139534949 true] [17592186321933 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534949 true] [17592186321933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534949 true] [17592186321933 1111 #uuid "5e1d2b69-f372-